{"availability":"available","full":"robenkleene/sidewinder","name":"sidewinder","description":"Euclidean sequencer for Max for Live that creates polyrhythms.","category":"Other","language":"Max","stars":26,"forks":2,"created":"2016-01-03T21:40:10Z","updated":"2026-10-03T10:29:08Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://maxforlive.com/library/device/5794/sidewinder","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:16.253Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:16.253Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:15:16.253Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:48.020Z","stars":26,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:58.973Z","stars":26,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:08:00.215Z","stars":26,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-11T07:23:37.575Z","stars":26,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:15:16.253Z","stars":26,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sidewinder is a Euclidean sequencer for Max for Live that creates polyrhythms. Sidewinder takes a number of pulses (notes) and positions them as equidistant as possible into a number of steps. Equidistant distribution is a key to creating rhythms that are inherently musical. Many traditional rhythms can be generated through this simple process, see the example rhythms section.","The Euclidean algorithm computes greatest common divisor of two numbers. Godfried Toussaint discovered its musical applications and published them in \"The Euclidean Algorithm Generates Traditional Musical Rhythms\". Applied to music, the algorithm takes k pulses (notes) and distributes them as equidistant as possible in n steps."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robenkleene/sidewinder/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"6c3a0acaef3aa56d646a41b00fb141175c614d163b3dc879044557cc23510d94","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:48.148Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T20:55:40.841Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Sidewinder is a Euclidean sequencer for